{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543663-v20-is-obfuscate-a-mind-affecting-effect","id":1543663,"title":"[V20] Is Obfuscate a mind affecting effect?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-12T20:30:55-07:00","id":1543663,"title":"[V20] Is Obfuscate a mind affecting effect?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> As per the title, in V20 is Obfuscate a mind affecting effect? this is for purposes of other gamelines powers that defend against such effects, such as Mind 1 defensive usages.<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-13-2024, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T23:49:01-07:00","id":1543669,"title":"","content":"Yes. While how to handle it in cross-overs is always going to be a bit complicated, as written Obfuscate is mental trickery, not physical illusions and the like. A common example is that cameras (not having minds) will record a character using Obfuscate to move unseen, even if someone watching the image on the camera's screen live doesn't see them in the moment (since that viewer has a mind and is still impacted).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T01:21:50-07:00","id":1543670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543663-v20-is-obfuscate-a-mind-affecting-effect?p=1543669#post1543669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. While how to handle it in cross-overs is always going to be a bit complicated, as written Obfuscate is mental trickery, not physical illusions and the like. A common example is that cameras (not having minds) will record a character using Obfuscate to move unseen, even if someone watching the image on the camera's screen live doesn't see them in the moment (since that viewer has a mind and is still impacted).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how it's framed in VDA20, even though it's not super clear: Obfuscate has an area of effect of 5 metres per dot of Wits+Stealth of the vampire (or something along these lines). That helps drive home the point that it's a mind trick and has limitations accordingly. In this way it can be imagined like a sort of psychic cloak cast on the minds of those within the area of effect, not those outside of it. It forces players to think carefully about when and where to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T12:08:30-07:00","id":1543697,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate is a mental power that at the basic level makes people not notice you and certainly the Awakened have defenses against this Discipline.<br /> <br /> It brings back a old Iron Man story where Tony Stark was up against The Masters of Silence who were cybertech ninjas that cloud people's minds but the guard snapped out of it when he saw them on the security monitor beside him and Iron Man's tech also bypassed that power in the rematch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-13-2024, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T16:12:57-07:00","id":1543713,"title":"","content":"Just to correct something:<br /> <br /> Obfuscate isn't a mind effect just in V20, it has always been. They may have changed it in V5, idk, but otherwise it's a Mind Effect in every edition, with or without limited area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T07:35:17-07:00","id":1543748,"title":"","content":"The fact that Obfuscate is a mental interaction rather than light bending or illusion means that security cameras do actually record a hidden vampire, it's just that anyone viewing it has to beat the Obfuscate rating to notice the vampire in the footage.<br /> <br /> In recent years this in turn suggests that AI facial recognition software would be able to find Obfuscated vampires in media since it doesn't have a mind, but the humans who manually review the footage wouldn't be able to perceive the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T20:29:41-07:00","id":1543821,"title":"","content":"As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, handling it in a crossover is a bit more complicated, so it would be interesting for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a> to say which interactions are on the table. But those complications usually boil down to &quot;if a power is meant to reveal secrets, it should get a shot&quot;. Mind 1 would depend a lot on how the Mage is using it, the particulars of the effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T10:20:39-07:00","id":1543885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543663-v20-is-obfuscate-a-mind-affecting-effect?p=1543821#post1543821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, handling it in a crossover is a bit more complicated, so it would be interesting for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a> to say which interactions are on the table. But those complications usually boil down to &quot;if a power is meant to reveal secrets, it should get a shot&quot;. Mind 1 would depend a lot on how the Mage is using it, the particulars of the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks,<br /> <br /> I was looking at the Mind 1 mental shield effect for a potential chronicle (we are not playing yet, just chekcing ideas here). It would be a Kitsune our social specialist, a Mage (me) with Correspondence, Mind, Prime and Entropy and we were thinking a Song of the Shadow ritualist... Our main <i>potential </i>antagonists are regular vampires so we were OOC discussing strategies, since we lack muscle, a blood pumped vampire is a threat... Specially someone that is Obfuscated and then axe/punch/kick to the head.<br /> <br /> We are considering rebalancing the Song of the Shadow for a Stargazer Ahroun as a muscle but it is not what we were looking for in this game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-15-2024, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T14:47:06-07:00","id":1543911,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, if you're worried about combat heavy hitters... how to handle Obfuscate isn't really the biggest concern. Any solid WoD combat character can do major damage regardless of surprise attacks.<br /> <br /> There are lots of options (including lots of options presented in official books over the years!), and which is best depends so much on factors that are really up to your group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T13:52:53-07:00","id":1544138,"title":"","content":"So in essence Obfuscate is a mental effect that is great if your playing detective style or espionage games when you don't want to be noticed or makings others see you as someone else or hiding items on your person or a bolt hole if your knowledge of the Discipline is very advanced. But I wouldn't use it in a straight up combat game myself as I don't see it as the best use for such a useful power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T16:12:32-07:00","id":1544148,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar727_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"727\" data-vbnamecard=\"727\">Thoth</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16965\" data-vbnamecard=\"16965\">Hermeticus</a><br /> <br /> First, thanks to all for answering.<br /> <br /> And we were hypothesizing some cases of what would happen to our favoured characters in combat. We are very aware that WoD is deadly, and our characters are not combat optimized, more Social (Kitsune) and Mental (myself), our third party member is the one that is looking either to be the muscle or to have some esoteric abilities; and among the many many scenarios we have discussed Obfuscate arised.<br /> <br /> We are painfully aware that as we are right now a single starting Garou can kill us in straight combat.<br /> <br /> And we were discussing 'What If?' Scenarios... What do we do if we get ambushed by Obfuscate and sucker punched? What happens if we get grappled by a Potence Cainite? What if we find a Celerity user?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-04-2026, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T12:36:51-07:00","id":1544305,"title":"","content":"In regards to Lupines my advice is unless your a member of the Ventrue, Gangrel or Banu Haqim clans, your best chance of survival is not encountering them or run like hell when you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T13:08:40-07:00","id":1544307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543663-v20-is-obfuscate-a-mind-affecting-effect?p=1544305#post1544305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to Lupines my advice is unless your a member of the Ventrue, Gangrel or Banu Haqim clans, your best chance of survival is not encountering them or run like hell when you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to have misunderstood. We are not Vampires, we are respectively a Kitsune (our social specialist), a mage (myself, mental tasks things for me) and we have two options for the third role either an Ahroun or a Song of the Shadow Kuei Jin (my friend has not yet decided).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T17:27:15-08:00","id":1557286,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16965\" data-vbnamecard=\"16965\">Hermeticus</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <br /> <br /> A bit of thread necromancy, but same question for Chimerstry on V20. Would its effects count as mind affecting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T19:12:56-08:00","id":1557291,"title":"","content":"Yep. Chimerstry has always been presented as creating mental illusions... though eventually it does blur the lines with the idea of illusions so real that could cause physical harm.<br /> <br /> In at least some editions (can't look up all of them to check right now) Chimestry has interesting crossover implications with Changeling as the illusions it creates can be counted as &quot;real&quot; to Chimerical reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T07:34:03-08:00","id":1557307,"title":"","content":"I agree. Both Obfuscate and Chimerstry are mind-affecting powers for purposes of other games\u2019 abilities (such as the Mind Sphere for Mage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T03:30:58-08:00","id":1557340,"title":"","content":"Indeed. This is even the very reason behind the idea of its illusions being real for Chimeric reality, Chimeras are all about mind, not perception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T01:43:02-08:00","id":1557406,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's a mind affecting power in the sense that it doesn't actually make you invisible. Rather it tricks the people around you into ignoring your presence.<br /> <br /> I don't remember which book I read this in, but there was mention about how even if the people don't know you're in the crowd, they will subconsciously move out of your way, as you attempt to maneuver through them. Meaning you don't need to worry about trying to squeeze and weave through a densely populated location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}